{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "NCEPNCARReanalysis",
    "description": "NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 regridding model — the coupler half of the ncep_ncar loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, esm-3nc.1 era5 pattern). Exposes 6-hourly pressure-level atmospheric variables (temperature, geopotential height, vertical velocity, horizontal winds) and static surface geopotential on the simulation's target grid.\n\nStructure (RFC §6): declares two pure-I/O loaders as subsystems — NCEPNCAR_Pressure (./ncep_ncar_pressure_loader.esm, time-varying) and NCEPNCAR_Surface (./ncep_ncar_surface_loader.esm, static) — and re-exposes their fields as model observeds (T, Z, omega, u, v, Z_sfc). Native grids are geographic (longlat/WGS84) → longlat identity reprojection (esd-47z.1). Regridding is per-variable (`regrid`): horizontal winds uwnd/vwnd → B-spline (esd-47z.3); centered scalars air/hgt/omega and the static hgt_sfc → conservative.\n\nData covers 1948–present at 2.5°×2.5° global resolution with 17 standard pressure levels (10–1000 hPa). Migrated from EarthSciData.jl src/NCEP-NCAR_Reanalysis.jl:224 (NCEPNCARReanalysis, esm-k3bb); split into pure loaders + regridding model by esm-3nc.2.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "reanalysis",
      "ncep",
      "ncar",
      "pressure_levels",
      "data_loader",
      "regridding_model",
      "longlat",
      "pure-io-split"
    ],
    "created": "2026-05-30T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "NOAA NCEP",
      "NCAR",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.2)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Kalnay, E., Kanamitsu, M., Kistler, R., Collins, W., Deaven, D., Gandin, L., Iredell, M., Saha, S., White, G., Woollen, J., Zhu, Y., Leetmaa, A., Reynolds, R., Chelliah, M., Ebisuzaki, W., Higgins, W., Janowiak, J., Mo, K. C., Ropelewski, C., Wang, J., Jenne, R., Joseph, D. (1996). The NCEP/NCAR 40-year reanalysis project. Bulletin of the American Meteorological Society, 77(3), 437–471.",
        "url": "https://psl.noaa.gov/data/gridded/data.ncep.reanalysis.html",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0477(1996)077<0437:TNYRP>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl src/NCEP-NCAR_Reanalysis.jl:4-66 (NCEPNCARReanalysisFileSet), :72-79 (relpath), :224 (NCEPNCARReanalysis constructor). Test: test/NCEP-NCAR_Reanalysis_test.jl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "NCEPNCARReanalysis": {
      "coupletype": "NCEPNCARReanalysisCoupler",
      "reference": {
        "notes": "This is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; esm-3nc.1 era5 pattern, bead esm-3nc.2). The pre-migration ncep_ncar.esm carried the NCEPNCARReanalysis coupler model AND two co-located data_loaders blocks: NCEPNCAR_Pressure (grid, 6-hourly time-varying pressure-level fields) and NCEPNCAR_Surface (static surface geopotential). Both are now pure-I/O files referenced as subsystems under their ORIGINAL names (NCEPNCAR_Pressure → ./ncep_ncar_pressure_loader.esm, NCEPNCAR_Surface → ./ncep_ncar_surface_loader.esm), so the observed expressions NCEPNCAR_Pressure.<var> and NCEPNCAR_Surface.hgt_sfc keep resolving unchanged. The removed co-located spatial/regridding sub-blocks become the loaders' GDD grid (longlat/WGS84) and the model's per-variable regrid.\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): both loaders' grid.crs.projection is 'longlat' (geographic WGS84), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1) — the IDENTITY transform.\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The horizontal wind components uwnd, vwnd → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3); the centered scalars air, hgt, omega (vertical-velocity scalar) and the static hgt_sfc → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm).\n\nsource_ref: EarthSciData.jl src/NCEP-NCAR_Reanalysis.jl:224\n\nUpstream constructor NCEPNCARReanalysis(domaininfo; kwargs...) creates an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon (rad), lat (rad), lev (hPa)\n  - One DataSetInterpolator per varnames(fileset): builds interp_unsafe equation for each NC variable\n  - Equation template (from create_interp_equation, pressure-level variables):\n      var(t) ~ interp_unsafe(data, fit, fi_lon, fi_lat, fi_lev, extrap)\n    where fit  = 1 + (t_ref + t - tstart) / tstep\n          fi_lon = 1 + (lon - lonstart) / lonstep\n          fi_lat = 1 + (lat - latstart) / latstep\n          fi_lev = 1 + (lev - levstart) / levstep\n  - Surface variable (hgt.sfc.nc, static): fi_time argument omitted, read once\n  - discrete_events: build_interp_event fires at 6-hourly tstops to reload pressure-level data buffers\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => NCEPNCARReanalysisCoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo)\n\ngt-p3ep resolution: the @register_symbolic interp_unsafe pattern is replaced by the data_loaders §8\nmechanism. NCEPNCAR_Pressure.* variables are loader outputs regridded from the 2.5°×2.5°/17-level grid\nto the model domain (lon, lat, lev) at each 6-hourly timestep. NCEPNCAR_Surface.hgt_sfc is the\nstatic surface geopotential height, read once. The runtime handles the build_interp_event discrete\ncallbacks implicitly via data_loaders.temporal.frequency = PT6H.\n\nParameter units: lon and lat are in radians (matching EarthSciML convention for MTK integration;\nthe NCEP NC files store longitude in degrees, conversion handled by the runtime regridder).\nlev is in hPa (matching the NCEP NC 'level' coordinate in millibars = hPa)."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. The runtime regridder converts radians to degrees for spatial interpolation against the NCEP 2.5°×2.5° grid."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. The runtime regridder converts radians to degrees for spatial interpolation."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "hPa",
          "default": 500.0,
          "description": "Pressure level (hPa). Corresponds to the 'level' coordinate in NCEP NC files. Standard levels: 1000, 925, 850, 700, 600, 500, 400, 300, 250, 200, 150, 100, 70, 50, 30, 20, 10 hPa. Coupled to the simulation domain's pressure coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Air temperature at the current grid point and pressure level (K). Interpolated in time (6-hourly), space (2.5°×2.5° → model domain), and pressure level from the NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 'air' variable.",
          "expression": "NCEPNCAR_Pressure.air"
        },
        "Z": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Geopotential height at the current grid point and pressure level (m). Interpolated in time (6-hourly), space, and pressure level from the NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 'hgt' variable.",
          "expression": "NCEPNCAR_Pressure.hgt"
        },
        "omega": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "Pa/s",
          "description": "Lagrangian tendency of pressure (vertical velocity in pressure coordinates) at the current grid point and pressure level (Pa/s). Interpolated from the NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 'omega' variable.",
          "expression": "NCEPNCAR_Pressure.omega"
        },
        "u": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Zonal (west–east) wind component at the current grid point and pressure level (m/s). Interpolated from the NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 'uwnd' variable.",
          "expression": "NCEPNCAR_Pressure.uwnd"
        },
        "v": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Meridional (south–north) wind component at the current grid point and pressure level (m/s). Interpolated from the NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 'vwnd' variable.",
          "expression": "NCEPNCAR_Pressure.vwnd"
        },
        "Z_sfc": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Surface geopotential height (m). Static field read once from the NCEP/NCAR Reanalysis 1 'hgt.sfc.nc' file. Spatially interpolated to the model domain; does not vary in time or pressure level.",
          "expression": "NCEPNCAR_Surface.hgt_sfc"
        }
      },
      "subsystems": {
        "NCEPNCAR_Pressure": {
          "ref": "./ncep_ncar_pressure_loader.esm"
        },
        "NCEPNCAR_Surface": {
          "ref": "./ncep_ncar_surface_loader.esm"
        }
      },
      "regrid": {
        "air": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Air temperature (K). Cell-centered scalar → conservative area-weighted overlap-join regridder (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm)."
        },
        "hgt": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Geopotential height (m). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder."
        },
        "omega": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Vertical velocity (Pa/s). A centered scalar (not a horizontal wind) → conservative regridder."
        },
        "uwnd": {
          "method": "bspline",
          "description": "Zonal wind component (m/s). Horizontal wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3). Re-exposed as model observed u; coupled to MeanWind.v_lon."
        },
        "vwnd": {
          "method": "bspline",
          "description": "Meridional wind component (m/s). Horizontal wind → B-spline interpolating regridder (esd-47z.3). Re-exposed as model observed v; coupled to MeanWind.v_lat."
        },
        "hgt_sfc": {
          "method": "conservative",
          "description": "Static surface geopotential height (m). Cell-centered scalar → conservative regridder."
        }
      },
      "equations": [],
      "tests": []
    }
  }
}
